      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "The network server and Python application have different roles. ASGI connects them through protocol events.",
          "role": "intro",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle#tb1"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [],
            "anchors": []
          },
          "block_id": "tile_009.s01.b01"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "The ASGI server handles the network connection and invokes the application callable through ASGI.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle#f1"
            ],
            "anchors": []
          },
          "block_id": "tile_009.s01.b02"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "The callable is async def app(scope, receive, send). scope describes the connection; receive and send exchange events. Receive http.request through receive(), then send http.response.start with status and headers, followed by http.response.body through send().",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "asgi.request_lifecycle#tb3"
            ],
